IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpc-dates`
IMPORT `lpc-core`
IMPORT `lpc-seat`

-- Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA), Schedule 3 -- cases for the client's seat (lpc-seat.l4). Every expected value was
-- worked by hand from the deposited text (the clause is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's output.
-- Edges: 30 June and 1 July 2014; the 28th and 29th day after being told of the right to notify; $1 500 and $1 500.01;
-- an uplift fee at exactly 25% and one cent over; 4 and 5 cooling-off business days, the 5th and 6th business day;
-- the 29th and 30th day after a bill (interest and proceedings); the 21st and 22nd day after a request; the last day
-- of the 6 months (month ends and 29 February); a reduction of exactly 15% and of 14.99%; a rate exactly at and just
-- over the Cash Rate Target plus 2. Cash Rate Target figures are invented test figures, not the Reserve Bank's series.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the client`

`SA`        MEANS `in South Australia`
`elsewhere` MEANS `in another Australian jurisdiction`
`unknown`   MEANS `it cannot be determined where`
`me`        MEANS `an individual, or a business or body not listed below`
`big co`    MEANS `a public company, a subsidiary of a public company, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a subsidiary of a foreign company or a registered Australian body`
`crown co`  MEANS `a corporation with share capital held mostly for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
`injury`    MEANS `another matter, for example a personal injury, compensation or other civil claim`
`migration` MEANS `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth`
`criminal`  MEANS `a criminal matter`
`direct`    MEANS `you and the law practice you retained`
`between firms` MEANS `your law practice and a law practice it retained for you`
`d`         MEANS `the date` 1 1 2000

§§ `cll 3, 4, 5: does Schedule 3 apply`

#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `SA` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you first instructed the law practice in the matter in South Australia (cl 3)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `SA` (`the date` 30 6 2014) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: you first instructed the law practice before Schedule 3 commenced on 1 July 2014`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `SA` (`the date` 1 7 2014) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you first instructed the law practice in the matter in South Australia (cl 3)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `elsewhere` (`the date` 1 8 2020) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `elsewhere` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 29 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `elsewhere` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 30 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: your notice was given more than 28 days after the law practice told you of your right to give it (cl 4(4))`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `elsewhere` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 30 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `elsewhere` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: neither clause 3 nor clause 4 makes this Schedule apply to the matter`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `SA` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no longer: the matter is connected with another jurisdiction and you chose that jurisdiction's costs law (cl 5)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `SA` (`the date` 1 8 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `d` `d` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you first instructed the law practice in the matter in South Australia (cl 3)`
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` `unknown` (`the date` 1 8 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `d` (`the date` 1 9 2020) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`

§§ `cll 9, 11, 13; reg 60: must costs be disclosed`

#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 1500 FALSE FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the total legal costs, excluding disbursements, are not likely to exceed $1 500 excluding GST; if the law practice learns they are likely to, it must disclose as soon as practicable (cl 13(1)(a), (2))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 1500.01 FALSE FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the law practice must disclose its costs to you in writing, before or as soon as practicable after it is retained (cll 10, 12)`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` TRUE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a barrister engaged for your matter need not disclose costs to you (cl 9)`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE TRUE 20000 FALSE FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a law practice retained for you by your own law practice discloses to that law practice, which discloses to you (cl 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 TRUE TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you had a disclosure in the previous 12 months and waived further disclosure in writing, and a principal decided on reasonable grounds that it was not warranted (cl 13(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 TRUE FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the law practice must disclose its costs to you in writing, before or as soon as practicable after it is retained (cll 10, 12)`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE `big co` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you are a client of a kind clause 13(1)(c) lists, a sophisticated client (cl 13(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE `me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the costs or their basis were agreed through a tender process (cl 13(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE `me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you will not be required to pay the costs, and they will not otherwise be recovered (cl 13(1)(e))`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` FALSE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE `crown co` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you are a corporation held for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory (cl 13(1)(f), reg 60)`

§§ `cl 18: a failure to disclose`

#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `clause 18 does not apply: the law practice disclosed everything Part 3 required`
#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; you may apply to set aside your costs agreement; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1)-(4))`
#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1), (2), (4))`
#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount; you may still apply to set aside your costs agreement (cl 18(1)-(3))`
#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount (cl 18(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `clause 18(1)-(4) do not apply to this law practice's own costs: it failed to disclose only because the law practice it retained for you did not give it the information (cl 18(5)(a))`

§§ `cl 19: reports`

#ASSERT `Can I be charged for a report from my law practice` `a written report of the progress of the matter` EQUALS `the law practice must give it on reasonable request, and may charge you a reasonable amount for it (cl 19(1)(a), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can I be charged for a report from my law practice` `a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill` EQUALS `no: the law practice must give it on reasonable request and must not charge you for it (cl 19(1)(b), (2))`

§§ `cll 25(2), 26(1a): which matters may be conditional`

#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `injury` EQUALS `yes: a conditional (no win, no fee) costs agreement may relate to this matter (cl 25(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `criminal` EQUALS `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a criminal matter (cl 25(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `a matter that relates to or involves child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption` EQUALS `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter involving child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption (cl 25(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 of the Commonwealth` EQUALS `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (cl 25(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `proceedings under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 of the Commonwealth` EQUALS `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (cl 25(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` `migration` EQUALS `yes, but without an uplift fee: a conditional costs agreement may relate to this matter, but not provide for an uplift fee (cll 25(2), 26(1a))`

§§ `cl 26: uplift fees`

#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` FALSE `injury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: an uplift fee may be provided for only in a conditional costs agreement (cll 1, 26(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` TRUE `criminal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter at all (cl 25(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` TRUE `migration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not in a conditional costs agreement for proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 (cl 26(1a))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` TRUE `injury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: in a litigious matter, only if the risk of the claim failing, and of your having to meet your own costs, is significant (cl 26(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: at most 25% of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable (cl 26(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` TRUE `injury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: Schedule 3 sets no maximum for a matter that is not litigious; the agreement must still identify the basis and estimate the fee (cl 26(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `What is the most uplift fee in a litigious matter` 40000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most uplift fee in a litigious matter` 12345 EQUALS 3086.25
#ASSERT `What is the most uplift fee in a litigious matter` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `cl 27: contingency fees`

#ASSERT `Can my lawyer charge a percentage of my compensation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `clause 27 does not apply: what you pay is not calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or property recovered`
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer charge a percentage of my compensation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `allowed to the extent that the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs (cl 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my lawyer charge a percentage of my compensation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a costs agreement may not calculate what you pay by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered; such an agreement is void and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter (cll 27(1), 29(1), (5))`

§§ `cll 24-27, 29(1), 51: is the agreement void`
-- The base case: a written, signed no win, no fee agreement for a personal injury claim in court, with an uplift fee of
-- $10 000 on $40 000 (exactly 25%) and a 5-business-day cooling-off period. Each case changes one or two facts.
-- Argument order: parties, kind of client, tender, writing, by conduct, offer statements, excludes adjudication,
-- conditional, matter, success defined, plain, signed, advice, cooling-off days, uplift, basis, estimate, litigious,
-- risk significant, uplift fee, costs otherwise payable, share of recovery, adopts scale.

#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000.01 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `migration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `migration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 50000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `big co` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is not signed by you (cll 25(3)(c)(iii), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `between firms` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it does not state that you were told of your right to independent legal advice (cll 25(3)(d), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it does not set out the circumstances that are the successful outcome (cll 25(3)(a), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is not in clear plain language (cll 25(3)(c)(ii), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it is not in writing or evidenced in writing (cll 24(2), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: a conditional costs agreement may not be accepted by conduct; it must be in writing (cll 24(3) note, 25(3)(c)(i), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it was accepted by conduct, but the offer did not clearly state that it was an offer to enter a costs agreement, that it could be accepted in writing or by conduct, and what conduct would accept it (cll 24(3), (4), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: it says the costs are not subject to adjudication, and you are not a sophisticated client who may contract out (cll 24(5), 29(1), 51)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `big co` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 5000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `criminal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter (cll 25(2), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `injury` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 20000 40000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `void, and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter: it is a contingency fee agreement (cll 27, 29(1), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is my costs agreement void` `direct` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 40000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`

§§ `cl 25(3)(e), (4)-(6): cooling off`
-- Argument order: conditional, kind of client, tender, between two law practices, period in the agreement, business
-- days so far.

#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE 5 5 EQUALS `yes: you may end it by written notice now; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before you ended it on your instructions and knowing it would be done in the cooling-off period, and no uplift fee (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE 5 6 EQUALS `no: the cooling-off period has ended`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE 5 0 EQUALS `yes: you may end it by written notice now; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before you ended it on your instructions and knowing it would be done in the cooling-off period, and no uplift fee (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE 10 7 EQUALS `yes: you may end it by written notice now; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before you ended it on your instructions and knowing it would be done in the cooling-off period, and no uplift fee (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE FALSE 4 1 EQUALS `the agreement is void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` FALSE `me` FALSE FALSE 0 1 EQUALS `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: the agreement is not a conditional costs agreement`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `big co` FALSE FALSE 0 1 EQUALS `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: you are a sophisticated client, or the agreement is between two law practices (cl 25(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` TRUE FALSE 0 1 EQUALS `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: you are a sophisticated client, or the agreement is between two law practices (cl 25(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `me` FALSE TRUE 0 1 EQUALS `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: you are a sophisticated client, or the agreement is between two law practices (cl 25(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` TRUE `crown co` FALSE FALSE 4 1 EQUALS `the agreement is void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`

§§ `cl 29(2)-(6): a void agreement`

`cl 27 void` MEANS `it is a contingency fee agreement (cl 27)`
`cl 26 void` MEANS `it breaches clause 26 (uplift fees)`
`other void` MEANS `it breaches another provision of Part 5`

#ASSERT `What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` `cl 27 void` 30000 40000 10000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` `cl 27 void` 30000 40000 10000 8000 EQUALS 8000
#ASSERT `What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` `cl 26 void` 30000 40000 10000 EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` `cl 26 void` 30000 40000 10000 45000 EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` `cl 26 void` 50000 40000 10000 EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` `cl 26 void` 50000 40000 10000 50000 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` `other void` 50000 40000 10000 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` `other void` 50000 40000 10000 45000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` `other void` 30000 40000 0 EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` `other void` 30000 40000 0 35000 EQUALS 5000

§§ `cl 30: setting aside`

#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement be set aside` FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to the Supreme Court; it may set the agreement aside only if satisfied that it is not fair and reasonable (cl 30(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my costs agreement be set aside` TRUE EQUALS `the Supreme Court may set it aside, and then order what you pay: the applicable scale, or fair and reasonable costs, never more than the agreement would have given (cl 30(1), (4)-(6))`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay after my costs agreement is set aside` 25000 20000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay after my costs agreement is set aside` 15000 20000 EQUALS 15000

§§ `cl 23, reg 61: interest (bill of 1 March 2025; Cash Rate Target 4.1, so at most 6.1)`

#ASSERT `May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 31 3 2025) 6.1 4.1 EQUALS `yes: the costs have been unpaid for 30 days or more after the bill (cl 23(1))`
#ASSERT `May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 30 3 2025) 6.1 4.1 EQUALS `not yet: interest may be charged only once the costs are unpaid 30 days or more after the bill, unless your costs agreement provides for it (cl 23(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 2 3 2025) 6 4.1 EQUALS `yes: your costs agreement provides for interest (cl 23(2))`
#ASSERT `May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 2 4 2025) 6.11 4.1 EQUALS `no: the rate is above the most the regulations allow, the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill plus 2 percentage points (cl 23(4), reg 61)`
#ASSERT `May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 2 4 2025) 5 4.1 EQUALS `no: the bill does not state that interest is payable and the rate (cl 23(3))`
#ASSERT `What is the highest interest rate my law practice may charge` 4.1 EQUALS 6.1
#ASSERT `What is the highest interest rate my law practice may charge` 3.85 EQUALS 5.85

§§ `cl 34: the itemised bill`

#ASSERT `By when must I get the itemised bill I asked for` (`the date` 10 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 31 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I get the itemised bill I asked for` (`the date` 25 12 2025) EQUALS `the date` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `Was my itemised bill given in time` FALSE (`the date` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 5 2025) (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `clause 34 does not apply: an itemised bill may be requested only after a bill that is not itemised (cl 34(1))`
#ASSERT `Was my itemised bill given in time` TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 31 3 2025) (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `in time: it was given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
#ASSERT `Was my itemised bill given in time` TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2025) (`the date` 1 5 2025) EQUALS `late: it was not given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
#ASSERT `Was my itemised bill given in time` TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2025) FALSE `d` (`the date` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `still in time: the 21 days after your request have not yet run out (cl 34(2))`
#ASSERT `Was my itemised bill given in time` TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2025) FALSE `d` (`the date` 1 4 2025) EQUALS `late: it was not given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`

§§ `cll 18(2), 31, 34(4)-(5), 44: being sued for costs (bill of 1 March 2025)`

#ASSERT `From what day may my law practice sue me for its costs` (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE `d` EQUALS `the date` 31 3 2025
#ASSERT `From what day may my law practice sue me for its costs` (`the date` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`the date` 20 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 19 4 2025
#ASSERT `May my law practice sue me for its costs on this day` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE `d` FALSE (`the date` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `yes: at least 30 days have passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `May my law practice sue me for its costs on this day` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE `d` FALSE (`the date` 30 3 2025) EQUALS `not yet: 30 days have not passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5)); a court must stay proceedings brought now (cl 31(3))`
